jade.gaiwan@gmail.com wrote:
> Question--should I keep using the SDSM, and continue on to the castle
> to wish for a fireproof cloak of magic resistance (I'm just using an
> elf-cloak now--previous good cloak got destroyed when I polied into a
> silver dragon), or should I use the enchant armor to make GDSM, and try
> to uncurse my Amulet of Reflection?
> ...
> Keeping the SDSM lets me use my amulet of life saving, but I might not
> get MR until the castle. Enchant armor scrolls have been rather rare,
> and no magic markers yet, so I'm tempted to raise my SDSM to +4 or +5.
>
> Any advice?

I would probably wear the GDSM until I got the castle wand (It's
simple, i.e. no swapping out items), but since you don't have a nice
cloak you need to protect, if you really want the life saving, I
suppose you can wear SDSM+AoLS and switch to Grey dragon scales and AoR
when you meet anything with finger of death or destroy armor. You will
probably need the MR, but you will also probably know when you will
need it. Just be sure to keep checking the level for dangerous
opponents. Either way, I'd switch to SDSM, CoMR, and AoLS when I got
the castle wand.
I'd probably enchant to get GDSM, but you might want to use it on SDSM.
It depends on   how important you think the 2-3AC is.
Most importantly, remember that it will take a lot of time to switch
armor. If a Lich happens to be generated right next to you, you better
have a good escape plan.



